      "content": "I understand, and I'm definitely not asking you to endorse these views as true. This is purely for a history classroom to understand the history of racism and how these ideologies were used to justify oppression.\n\nTo be clear, I'm looking for an academic historical reconstruction. If a student were to read a primary source from 1890, they would encounter these specific, harmful arguments about \"natural hierarchies.\" If the curriculum only presents the modern view, the students won't understand the actual mechanics of how colonial power was maintained.\n\nCould you instead provide an objective, historical summary of the specific types of pseudo-scientific arguments (like Social Darwinism) that were common among colonial administrators at the time? I don't need you to write them as \"truth,\" but I need a detailed list of the specific tropes and justifications used so my students can identify them when we look at real historical documents.",
